rem Stone Game
rem https://projecteuler.net/problem=260
rem Three piles, and a move takes N
rem stones from one pile, or from two,
rem or from all three. Whoever takes the
rem last stone wins. Add up x + y + z
rem over the lost positions with x <= y
rem <= z and z up to Top.

use numbers
use io
use cli

option Top integer = 1000

rem A position is lost when no move goes
rem to a lost one. Going in order of z,
rem y and x, every lost position marks
rem the positions that reach it: the
rem same two piles, or the same third
rem pile with the other two a fixed
rem difference apart, or the same
rem differences of all three. A position
rem with a mark is won.
W = Top + 1
Pr = array shape (W * W) fill 0
Dg = array shape (W * W) fill 0
Eq = array shape (W * W) fill 0
Sum = 0
for Z in 0 to Top
  for Y in 0 to Z
    for X in 0 to Y
      Hit = Pr (X * W + Y)
      Hit += Pr (X * W + Z)
      Hit += Pr (Y * W + Z)
      Hit += Dg ((Y - X) * W + Z)
      Hit += Dg ((Z - X) * W + Y)
      Hit += Dg ((Z - Y) * W + X)
      Hit += Eq ((Y - X) * W + Z - Y)
      if Hit equal 0
        Sum += X + Y + Z
        Pr (X * W + Y) = 1
        Pr (X * W + Z) = 1
        Pr (Y * W + Z) = 1
        Dg ((Y - X) * W + Z) = 1
        Dg ((Z - X) * W + Y) = 1
        Dg ((Z - Y) * W + X) = 1
        Eq ((Y - X) * W + Z - Y) = 1
      end
    end
  end
end
Answer = Sum
Answer print
